# Block_Connections.mmd

## Purpose
The typed graph of connections between the locations of a single block - one functional
quarter of a DANGEROUS region. The location tier, and the only tier that carries connection
type.

## Context
Read first:
- `GENRE.md`
- this region's `Locations.md` and its block-existence diagram (`setting/region/[Code]/Connections.mmd`)
- every block diagram already written for this region, for edges declared into this block

## Instructions
One file per block, `setting/region/[Region Code]/[Block Name].mmd`. DANGEROUS regions only;
SAFE and WILD regions carry a single region diagram instead, per `templates/Region_Connections.mmd`.

**Membership is stated, not inferred.** The `Locations:` header names every location this
block owns. It has to be explicit: a cross-block edge puts the far location's node in this
file too, so which block a node appears in cannot by itself say which block owns it. Every
code in the header has a node in the diagram, and every location belongs to exactly one
block in the region.

**Locations connect only to locations.** A location never connects to a block, a region, or
the setting. Every edge here has a location at both ends.

**Confirm before writing, and match what you confirm.** The region's block-existence diagram
says which blocks this one connects to, and blocks already written may declare edges into
this one. Both are read before the first edge is drawn. A cross-block edge is declared in
**both** block files and must be identical in all three of existence, type and direction -
a one-way edge reads `A --> B` in both files, never reversed to suit the far end's point of
view.

Connection type reference - the four kinds, per `patterns/dangerous/Door.md`:
- `A --- B` open - a two-way passage
- `A -.- B` secret - concealed, sealed, or needing a trigger to reveal
- `A --> B` one-way - traversable only in the direction shown
- `A ---|vertical| B` vertical - a climb, shaft, or drop between levels

A gate or a condition on an edge is stated in its label (`A ---|gated: forge rod| B`), not as
a fifth kind.

## Template
```
Block: [Block Name]
Purpose: [purpose family, per patterns/dangerous/Dressing.md - Keeping, Working, Living,
Holding, Meeting, Believing, Dying, or Moving]
Region: [Region Code] [Region Name]
Rooms: [room budget]
Locations: [every location code belonging to this block, comma separated]
```

```mermaid
graph LR
    A1["[Code] [Location Name]"] --- A2["[Code] [Location Name]"]
    A2 -.- A3["[Code] [Location Name]"]
    A3 --> A4["[Code] [Location Name]"]
    A4 ---|vertical| B7["[Code] [Location Name]"]
```
